A||||2||x-thumpr-x||Think I got a tranny problem.. Hmmm||||1||
Z||000000||x-thumpr-x||12-24-2001||07:32 PM||||On the highway this afternoon, my GT started stumbling abit like it's missing on one cylinder, my oil pressure is fine and  temp running around 55 celciuos. I get to my destination and check out the engine and it's running fine.  1 1/2 hrs go by and I go back and check my tranny fluid (manual). I pull out the speedo gear and there's no gear attached to it! (uh-oh) Fluid level is fine, so I stick my finger in, NOTHING THERE!  Plus the fluid is still alittle warm. <P>I recently pulled the tranny off the car to replace the though-out bearing and clutch fork. When I drained the tranny, it had automatic transmission fluid in it. Phoned a couple of shops and they said the fluid should be fine in that tranny, SO after re-installing the tranny, I filled it back up with the same fluid. Still a small amount of old fluid left in it and I didn't want to mix 5W30 with it.  Now, I'm missing a speedo gear (melted or dissintigrated) and think the fluid doesn't feel as thick either. <P>has anyone else had this problem before? suggestions on what to do? <BR>Gonna drain it and put 5W30 in like it supposed to have and find a new (used) gear. Pray no damage to the gears (hopefully) ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||12-25-2001||01:59 AM||||You were runing auto transmission fluid in a fiero manual? Also sounds like you have a little round gear floating around too. I'm just pointing out the obvious  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>Drain it and fill it with cheap 5w-30 and drive it aruound for 10 mins or something. Then drain it again and put in a quality 5w-30, or even try GM synchomesh (¿sp?).<P>If its as bad as you said though, you probably have some damage that cant be fixed. Maybe skip on the symcromesh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, I heard that stuff is expensive.<P>Good luck!!!!||||reg||11
Z||000002||StuGood||12-25-2001||03:30 PM||||The tranny fluid <B>won't</B> feel very thick, if it's ATF.  FWIW, 1986 manual recommends 5W-30 engine oil for the 4-speed transaxle.  I infer that you have a 1985 or 1986 GT with 4-speed Muncie (no separate dipstick).<P>I'm thinking it's possible the engine running poorly could be due to no VSS input?  I assume also that the speedometer quit during your drive.  Just guessing, here.<P>Finally, as far as finding a replacement goes, the VSS (speedo) gear is color-coded.  For example, my 1986 4-speed has a blue (30-tooth) VSS gear, P/N 25519845, to go with the "M17" 4-speed Muncie, 3.65 final drive ratio.  "M17" option code appears on the big sticker in the front compartment, LHS.  All this assumes everything is stock (original trans., etc.)<P>Point is, if you can fish- or drain-out the (remains of the) old gear, even if it's in pieces, the color may help you find a matching replacement.  Good luck (if you're really lucky, maybe you'll even find it intact)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     ||||reg||1
